  {
   "id": "concept1",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Production function; short run and long run"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "A production function gives the maximum quantity of output a firm can produce from each combination of inputs, with a given technology: $q = f(L, K)$. In the short run at least one input (say capital, K) is fixed, so output changes only by changing the variable input (labour, L). In the long run all inputs can be varied. An isoquant joins input combinations that give the same output."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "q = f(L, K) with given technology"
    },
    {
     "en": "Short run: some input fixed"
    },
    {
     "en": "Long run: all inputs variable"
    },
    {
     "en": "Isoquant: same output, different input mixes"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "A production function links inputs to the maximum output. In the short run some inputs are fixed; in the long run all inputs can change.",
    "kn": "ಉತ್ಪಾದನಾ ಫಲನವು ಆದಾನಗಳು ಮತ್ತು ಗರಿಷ್ಠ ಉತ್ಪನ್ನದ ಸಂಬಂಧ ತೋರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. ಅಲ್ಪಾವಧಿಯಲ್ಲಿ ಕೆಲವು ಆದಾನಗಳು ಸ್ಥಿರ; ದೀರ್ಘಾವಧಿಯಲ್ಲಿ ಎಲ್ಲವೂ ಬದಲಾಗಬಹುದು."
   },
   "formula": "q = f(L, K)"
  },
